{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation (read-only, 2026-11-12 ~05:55 PST)\nThe spend-cap Lambda (`/aws/lambda/bedrock-spend-cap` log, ticks from 13:41Z onward) reported the metered (ceiling-priced CloudWatch token) estimate at about 3 times the Cost Explorer figure for the same UTC day, with `effective_source=metered`. The metered arm crossed the daily threshold and attached `BedrockDailySpendCapDeny` (about 05:40 PST), denying `bedrock:InvokeModel` to every capped role, including rebar-gerrit-instance-role, until the 00:00 UTC release.\n\ninfra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/README.md documents the metered arm as an intentional upper bound, running at about 1.1 to 1.9 times settled billing. A ratio of about 3 is outside that band. Dollar figures are deliberately omitted (public tracker); they are in the Lambda log lines and Cost Explorer for 2026-11-12.\n\n## Root cause (measured; see comment)\nMost of the 3x was same-day Cost Explorer lag (re-read later, the 11-12 ratio is 1.94). The settled 2026-11-11 account-wide ratio is 2.04: the ceilings are tied to the 4.x price list, and for Opus 5.5 the cache-read ceiling is 3.125x the billed rate (other directions 1.5625x), with cache reads about 88% of Opus tokens. The ceilings still match their written definition; the documented band is stale.\n\n## Approach (decided 2026-11-12: README-only)\nUpdate `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/README.md`, ratios only:\n- Replace the 1.1-1.9x band with the measured band for the 5.5 generation, labelled by what each end is: about 1.8x for the Opus-only mix (lower end) to about 2.1x account-wide, where Sonnet traffic priced at the Opus ceilings raises it. State that cache reads drive the excess above 1.56x.\n- Explain that a same-day Cost Explorer comparison overstates the ratio because Cost Explorer lags intra-day (the \"about 3x\" sighting), so the comparison must use settled days.\nNo change to the handler, threshold, attachment, or Terraform. A per-model exact-match rate table remains a possible future story (not filed): it is a new mechanism, out of scope for a bug fix.\n\n## Testing\nExtend `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py` (which already pins README content via `README_PATH`), ratios only, no new price data:\n- Read `CEILING` from `handler.py` with `ast` (already public). Encode only the Opus 5.5 ceiling-over-billed factors (1.5625 input/output/cache-write, 3.125 cache-read) and the 2026-11-11 Opus token-direction shares (input 0.0089, output 0.0194, cache read 0.8763, cache write 0.0954).\n- Compute ratio = Σ_d share_d·CEILING_d ÷ Σ_d share_d·(CEILING_d / factor_d), i.e. the factors weighted by each direction's billed-dollar share (about 1.82), and assert the README band's lower end is at or below it and its upper end at or above the measured account-wide 2.04, with the band inside [min factor, max factor].\n- Assert the README states the 1.56x and 3.1x factors, that cache reads drive the excess, and the same-day-lag / settled-day guidance.\nThese fail on the current README. `make verify` passes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] [non-codebase] The ratio for 2026-11-12 is re-measured against the SETTLED Cost Explorer day, and the cause of any excess over the documented band is identified from the per-direction token counts.\n  provenance: environment=AWS 896586841071 Cost Explorer and CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock (us-east-1); principal=frontier profile; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — ce get-cost-and-usage by service and usage type plus per-ModelId get-metric-data token sums for 2026-11-11 and 2026-11-12; ratios recorded in ticket comments, figures in operator-local notes\n- [x] Either the ceiling table is corrected or the README band is updated with the measured reason; no config key, env var or flag."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794530821316406971,"uuid":"1ce64f29-c3dd-4be4-88ba-96e8caf6228a"}